qc.summary:
The 1080p final is usable to build on, but only after the specks are retouched. It is the same take as the draft, frame for frame.

**Same take.** Both clips are 97 frames at 24 fps. The best per-frame match against the draft is at the same index throughout the active motion, and the droplet and crown positions agree within 7 px.

**What the 1080p shows:**
- The ice is crisp and stays rigid, the ribs and camera are locked, and the crown at n12-n20 looks premium.
- The 480p draft hid a lot of dark speckling. It starts at n0, which is earlier than R3-18b's n12-n29 range:
  - two small dark dots on the left wall in n0-n19;
  - a dark oval in the coffee on the right in n0-n11;
  - a near-black central pearl in n12-n20, up to 60x24 px, including the cover frame n12;
  - an upper pearl in n17-n24;
  - an S-shaped streak in n20-n29;
  - a dark bean in the coffee in every settled frame, n60-n96.
- Exact frames, positions and sizes are in F1 and F4.
- Compression is acceptable. The flat backdrop is almost noise-free, so the 8-bit export needs dither or light grain to avoid banding.

**Gates on the final:**
- Gate 1 fails as written (SSIM 0.930 against the still); using n2 at f0 fixes it.
- Gates 2, 3 and 6 pass.
- Gates 4a, 4b, 5, 7 and 8 pass only with the remap, plates and retouch. Gate 4b starts failing at n16, not n21 as gates.json says.

**Hook preview (hookF/hook.mp4, R3-17 cut), seen as on a phone:**
- The first second does stop the thumb: loud lime-on-tangerine type, falling ice, impact at about f5 and the crown up by f10. Nothing fights the type; the droplets stop about 50 px below the tag.
- Its last third (f22-f29) shows the flat sheet wider than the glass that the owner has already rejected.
- The punch-in makes the dark pearls in the milk easy to see.

**Which cut to build.** The repo's R3-21 cut replaces R3-17 and ends on the crown's peak; it is the one to build. Before building it:
- retouch n2-n18 (and n0-n3 if the iris uses them) plus the tail bean;
- keep the n96 top plate;
- extend the floor plate into the shadow;
- add dither or grain.

No credits were spent and nothing in the repository was changed. That includes tash/HANDOFF.md, which I left alone because the task is read-only.

